    'a_part1_is_one_product_s_idp_it_holds_isolated_part2_pa_c2f6b974' => 'A :part1 is one product\'s IdP. It holds isolated :part2 :part3 — production and sandbox — each with its own users, keys and sign-in, and is billed on its own plan.',
    'a_part1_key_you_can_compose_into_roles_e_g_part2_part3_2714a35b' => 'A :part1 key you can compose into roles — e.g. :part2.:part3 :part4',
    'a_permission_is_one_thing_a_role_is_allowed_to_do_creat_522b0034' => 'A permission is one thing a role is allowed to do — "create invoices", "read reports". You can write your own here, without any code, and then compose them into roles. Apps can also register theirs automatically, so the list stays in step with what the app actually enforces. Permissions you write belong to you; the ones your environment shares are yours to use but not to change.',
    'a_permission_is_what_a_part1_may_do_once_signed_in_what_d4afab64' => 'A permission is what a :part1 may do, once signed in. What an :part2 may ask for is a scope, set when you register it under :part3 :part4 .',
    'a_permission_key_is_two_words_joined_by_a_colon_a_featu_b830fc34' => 'A permission key is two words joined by a colon — a feature and an action, like invoices:create.',
    'a_permission_with_that_key_already_exists_here_fa53c60f' => 'A permission with that key already exists here.',
    'a_phone_with_the_authenticator_app_installed_becomes_th_caef4b54' => 'A phone with the authenticator app installed becomes the thing that answers approval requests and tells you when someone signs in as you. Enrol it once by scanning the code; remove it here the moment you lose the handset, which stops it approving anything.',
    'a_project_is_one_idp_product_this_organization_owns_and_d87379c8' => 'A project is one IdP product this organization owns, and it is what environments hang off — so until the organization creates one from its own console, there is nothing here to target or open. Nothing on this screen creates one on the organization\'s behalf.',
    'a_project_is_one_of_your_products_with_its_own_plan_sig_45d566d1' => 'A project is one of your products, with its own plan, sign-in and environments such as production and staging. Open an environment from here to administer it, and create a new project when you launch a product that should be billed and run on its own.',
    'a_publishable_key_lets_a_page_sign_people_in_without_a_f1562297' => 'A publishable key lets a page sign people in without a backend of your own. It is public on purpose — what stops anybody else using it is the list of origins you allow it from.',
